de 4,8 a 7,1. En diciembre se adjudicó el 7 % de los contratos junto al límite, mientras que diciembre supone el 5 % de todos sus contratos de servicios y suministros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 113 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.986,50 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: La concentración de contratos en diciembre no indica malas prácticas. Puede ser debido a demandas estacionales o a presupuestos cerrados. El número de adjudicatarios no refleja responsabilidad individual.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos de diciembre se repartieron por necesidades distintas. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en áreas similares. Analizar si los contratos de diciembre se ajustaron a presupuestos específicos.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 244 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 41.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 5.8, with a 95% confidence interval of 4.8 to 7.1. December accounts for 7% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 5% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 67. Contract [1], for 14,986.50 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The high ratio of contracts just under the limit does not prove improper actions. It could reflect market conditions or budget constraints. Legal limits are strict, but small differences may result from standard pricing or separate needs.\nWhat can be checked: Check if multiple contracts cover the same service to avoid duplication. Review awardee A's contracts to see if they repeat the same requests. Contract [1] shows a single small purchase, which may be legitimate.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B 